; pos=yes warn=6
*fix 1 0 0 0
*data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino backclino
1 2a 10.00 001.5 178.5 01 01
1 2b 10.00 358.5 181.5 01 01

*data normal from to tape backtape compass backcompass clino backclino
1 5a 10.03 9.97 000 180 01 01
1 5b 10.04 9.96 359 181 01 01
1 5c 10.00 - 000 180 01 01
1 5d - 10.00 000 180 01 01

*calibrate backcompass 10
*data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino backclino
1 3a 10.00 001.5 188.5 01 01
1 3b 10.00 358.5 191.5 01 01

*calibrate compass 10
*calibrate backcompass 0
*data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino backclino
1 4a 10.00 011.5 178.5 01 01
1 4b 10.00 008.5 181.5 01 01

*data cartesian from to dx dy dz
; Work around variation in which station is picked for the maximum:
1 max 9 12 36

; Test that calibrating backcompass and backclino to measure forwards is
; handled suitably - this should not warn:
*calibrate compass 0
*calibrate clino 0
*calibrate backcompass 180
*calibrate backclino 0 -1
*data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino backclino
1 6a 10.00 90 90 10 10
; This seems to give bogus error:
; back2.svx:38:16: error: Plumbed CLINO and BACKCLINO readings can't be in the same direction
; 1 x 5 - - down down
;           ^~~~
; Also could extend context to cover both readings

*data normal from to tape compass clino
; create a single south-most point to avoid platform-dependent test output.
1 southmost 5 180 00
1 lowest 5 -down
